Original (sha256 f83d876da95472a013aac778d27c8130590739cc84d5a56046c078d26b4a2628):

pub fn last_index(len: usize) -> usize {
    len
}

Corrected file (sha256 c7c78b8ac7d84bc3dcd2781e56f6bfee81cbbf59af2ae7d16c186605fb5dd297, 69 bytes):

pub fn last_index(len: usize) -> usize {
    len.saturating_sub(1)
}

Exact change: single line in the function body, "-    len" replaced by "+    len.saturating_sub(1)", so a length of n now yields the last valid index n-1 (and len 0 saturates to 0 instead of underflowing). 1 line added, 1 line removed; function signature unchanged.
